.TH CHMAP_GET_PTR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chmap_get_ptr \- get pointer to value by key (type-safe)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chashmap.h>

value_ptr = chmap_get_ptr(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe wrapper for chmap_get_elem_ref() that returns a pointer to the
value, or NULL if key not found. Unlike chmap_get(), does not terminate
on key_not_found.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  Hash map to search
key      Key to look up
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to value if key found
Returns NULL if key not found
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Returns NULL if key not found (does not terminate)
Terminates program if value size doesn't match type size
Returns pointer to value for in-place modification
Pointer is correctly aligned for the value's type regardless of which
internal backend the map uses
Pointer invalidated by later insert/delete/resize operations
For strings, returns pointer to the char* itself
For a float or double key, see chmap_construct(3) for the map's
key equality contract (bitwise, except -0.0 canonicalized to 0.0)
For a long double key, see chmap_construct(3) for the map's key
equality contract (value-based, unlike every other key type)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chmap_construct(map, int, int);
chmap_insert(map, 42, 100);
int* ptr = chmap_get_ptr(map, 42);
if (ptr) {
  *ptr = 200; // Modify in-place
}
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_get (3),
.BR chmap_get_elem_ref (3),
.BR chmap_construct (3)
